        return q('Bilinear-transform Butterworth design', `Design a second-order digital Butterworth low-pass filter with sample rate fs = ${fs} Hz and −3 dB cutoff fc = ${fc} Hz, using the bilinear transform s = 2fs(1 − z⁻¹)/(1 + z⁻¹) with frequency prewarping. Write the result as H(z) = b₀(1 + 2z⁻¹ + z⁻²)/(1 + a₁z⁻¹ + a₂z⁻²). Find the prewarped analogue cutoff, the coefficients and the pole radius. Then find the gain at 2fc and compare it with the analogue prototype’s −12.3 dB. Also find the group delay at DC in samples.`, [`fs = ${fs} Hz`, `fc = ${fc} Hz`, 'Order 2, Butterworth', 'Bilinear transform with prewarping'], [p('Prewarped cutoff Ωc', Wc, 'rad/s'), p('Coefficient b₀', b0, ''), p('Coefficient a₁', a1, ''), p('Coefficient a₂', a2, ''), p('Pole radius', r, ''), p(`Gain at ${2 * fc} Hz`, hdb, 'dB'), p('Group delay at DC', gd, 'samples')], ['Prewarp: Ωc = 2fs·tan(πfc/fs). Let K = tan(πfc/fs).', 'Substitute s into Ωc²/(s² + √2Ωcs + Ωc²) and normalise by 1 + √2K + K². The poles are a complex pair with radius √a₂.', 'Evaluate H(e^(jω)) at ω = 2π·2fc/fs. For group delay, differentiate the unwrapped phase at ω → 0, analytically or with a small finite difference.'], [`K = ${fmt(K)}; Ωc = ${fmt(Wc)} rad/s.`, `b₀ = K²/(1 + √2K + K²) = ${fmt(b0)}; a₁ = 2(K² − 1)/(…) = ${fmt(a1)}; a₂ = (1 − √2K + K²)/(…) = ${fmt(a2)}.`, `Pole radius = √a₂ = ${fmt(r)}, angle ±${fmt(deg(Math.acos(-a1 / (2 * r))))}°.`, `|H| at ${2 * fc} Hz = ${fmt(hdb)} dB, compared with ${fmt(analog)} dB for the analogue prototype. Frequency warping compresses the response towards Nyquist.`, `Group delay at DC = ${fmt(gd)} samples = ${fmt(gd / fs * 1e6)} µs.`], 'Prewarping pins one frequency exactly. Everything else is warped by the tangent map, so the stopband steepens towards Nyquist.', hardBlock(`Digital Butterworth · fs = ${fs} Hz · fc = ${fc} Hz`, 'x[n] → b₀(1 + 2z⁻¹ + z⁻²) / (1 + a₁z⁻¹ + a₂z⁻²) → y[n]'), 'Bilinear transform; frequency warping; IIR filter coefficients; group delay.');
